INT. CASINO BASEMENT - COUNTING ROOM - NIGHT

A windowless vault of stainless steel counters and humming money counters. Stacks of bills in rubber bands. A camera dome on the ceiling blinks green.

NOVA, 30s, in a black security uniform with a mismatched badge, pushes a cart of laundry through the door. Her gait is bored and easy. She parks the cart, picks up a clipboard, and begins to count towels.

At the far counter, FELIX, 50s, the night supervisor, sits in a swivel chair eating a sandwich. He glances at her once, then returns to his sandwich.

She does not look at him. She walks the length of the room, adjusts a stack of towels, nudges a bill-counter's cover straight, checks the clipboard. She is just a woman doing a dull job.

FELIX
You're new.

NOVA
Third week.

FELIX
They don't send laundry down this late.

NOVA
They do when the fountain overflows.

He considers this. Swivels, chews. She keeps counting.

FELIX
Which one of the fountains?

NOVA
Lobby. The big one.

FELIX
The big one doesn't overflow.

NOVA
Tell that to the lobby.

Felix puts down the sandwich. He wipes his fingers on a napkin, one at a time. His hand drifts toward a desk phone and stops. She notices, and for an instant her bored mask slips and slides back.

She walks to the cart, reaches under the towels, and withdraws not a towel but a short black cylinder. She turns, thumb on a pin, smiling at him as one smiles at a toddler.

NOVA (CONT'D)
Felix. Don't.

FELIX
(very still)
How do you know my name?

NOVA
It's on your lanyard.

His eyes drop to the lanyard. They come up again. He lifts both hands slowly from the desk, and Nova steps closer, the cylinder held low, almost gently, as the camera dome on the ceiling blinks from green to red.

FELIX (CONT'D)
That camera...

NOVA
I know. I've been waiting for it.

She tosses the cylinder underhand onto his desk. It rolls to a stop against the sandwich, and Felix flinches. Nothing happens. It is only a flashlight.

Nova laughs, quietly, and wheels the cart toward the vault door, which clicks open from the other side.
